                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="485230" author="yujian" created="Sat, 24 Jan 2026 08:11:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+1 on master: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/4e4a5d72-a76a-43a9-8391-72b03b79e333&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/4e4a5d72-a76a-43a9-8391-72b03b79e333&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="486089" author="simmonsja" created="Sat, 31 Jan 2026 01:34:29 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I tested this locally and it passed. Are you still seeing failures?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I do see&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;obd_mount.c:230:lustre_add_mgc_failnodes()) MGC2601:8c1:c100:4ac0::32f4@tcp: can&apos;t add failover NID 2601:8c1:c100:4ac0:71a3:6be1:61c2:8dd2@tcp, rc = -75&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lustre_add_mgc_failnodes() breaks by copying NID into an obd_uuid so it gets truncated and then calls indirectly client_import_add_conn(). We really should be calling client_import_add_nids_to_conn().&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491641" author="nangelinas" created="Sat, 21 Mar 2026 18:25:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+1 on master for sanity/test27_cb and some similar tests: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5fed41d5-7f50-4526-9761-eebf0eda72b9&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5fed41d5-7f50-4526-9761-eebf0eda72b9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="491759" author="adilger" created="Mon, 23 Mar 2026 23:12:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This failed 25x in the past week (all running review-dne-ipv6, none running IPv4 testing):&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?horizon=518400&amp;amp;status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=0b0644d0-7d4b-11e7-a170-5254006e85c2&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/search?horizon=518400&amp;amp;status%5B%5D=FAIL&amp;amp;test_set_script_id=f9516376-32bc-11e0-aaee-52540025f9ae&amp;amp;sub_test_script_id=0b0644d0-7d4b-11e7-a170-5254006e85c2&amp;amp;source=sub_tests#redirect&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One test has console logs starting with messages like:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/b6c1100c-fa38-41c4-9378-f6de64f890bf&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/b6c1100c-fa38-41c4-9378-f6de64f890bf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;[ 1037.333479] LNet: 1 local NIs in recovery (showing 1): fd33:3981:3213:f020:0:5254:d6:f1f2@tcp
[ 1255.310620] Autotest: Test running for 20 minutes (lustre-reviews_review-dne-ipv6_122825.77)
[ 1555.888780] Autotest: Test running for 25 minutes (lustre-reviews_review-dne-ipv6_122825.77)
[ 1805.333492] LNet: 1 local NIs in recovery (showing 1): fd33:3981:3213:f020:0:5254:d6:f1f2@tcp
[ 1856.632576] Autotest: Test running for 30 minutes (lustre-reviews_review-dne-ipv6_122825.77)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;then proceed to eventually time out sanity, then run sanity-lnet.  Unfortunately, there aren&apos;t good logs about what happens before OST0000 goes offline and the test times out...&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another one has better logs at the start, but ends up with the same &lt;tt&gt;local NIs in recovery&lt;/tt&gt; message until the test times out:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/bb7c6359-cfa5-4b0e-ab1d-ef325736163a&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/bb7c6359-cfa5-4b0e-ab1d-ef325736163a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I don&apos;t see anything in the logs that indicate OST0000 is offline, but that is essentially what the test is reporting - that it cannot create files on OST0000.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It might be worthwhile to add some debugging to the error branch of test_27cb to run &lt;tt&gt;lfs df &amp;amp;&lt;/tt&gt; and a few more checks to see if the client and MDSes can communicate to OST0000.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
